<!--
  CAVERNS_PARITY_BUILD_1 — the eleven Deep flora, replacing the borrowed
  BMT_* wildPlants list of BMT_CrystalCaverns one for one
  (caverns_replacement_scoping.md §2, "flora" row).

  🔑 Three deliberate departures from the donor XML, all forced by the retirement
  and all recorded here so nobody "fixes" them back:

  1. **Vanilla parents, vanilla thingClass.** The donor hangs these off
     BMT_CavePlantBase / BMT_CaveBushBase / BMT_CaveTreeBase and gives two of them
     thingClass BMT.BiomesPlant. Both the parents and that Type die with the donor,
     and a ThingDef whose ParentName or thingClass cannot resolve is discarded, so
     these hang off vanilla PlantBase / BushBase / TreeBase with thingClass Plant.
     BMT.BiomesPlant adds the donor's own pollution/temperature handling; the
     temperature fields it read are set directly on the defs below instead.

  2. **Harvest products are vanilla where the donor's were its own.** The donor's
     BMT_MushroomLog becomes WoodLog and BMT_MycelialBlocks is dropped (mycelium
     becomes pure ground cover, purpose Misc). Grey Lady already harvested vanilla
     Cloth and still does; dulcis harvests RotSporeKit's RUT_RawDulcis
     (DEEP_DULCIS_DEDUP_1, owner ruling 2026-09-18 — RotSporeKit owns raw dulcis,
     this mod no longer ships its own RUT_DeepRawDulcis).

  3. **No research or fungiponics gates.** sowResearchPrerequisites
     BMT_ResearchMushrooms and the BMT_Fungiponics sowTag are donor defs. Sowing
     these is gated by skill only until we ship a fungiponics line of our own;
     that is an owed item, not a defect.

  UNMEASURED: the donor's Biomes_PlantControl modExtension on luminous spout
  (terrainTags Water/Fresh/Shallow/Boggy/Marshy) is a BiomesCore Type. Replaced
  with vanilla wildTerrainTags, which is the nearest vanilla mechanism; whether
  the two place hydrophytes identically has not been measured in game.
-->
